---
import Feature from "../../layouts/Feature.astro"
import Beat from "../../components/Beat.astro"
import Term from "../../components/Term.astro"
import { localDomain } from "../../site"

const faq = [
  {
    q: "Do I still need SSH keys?",
    a: "Not to manage. Paperboat creates and rotates the key it uses and installs it on the machines you may reach. You never edit authorized_keys or send a public key to a colleague.",
  },
  {
    q: "Does VS Code Remote-SSH work?",
    a: `Yes. Connect to the machine's host name, for example <code>studio.${localDomain}</code>. Cursor, Zed and anything else that reads your SSH config work the same way.`,
  },
  {
    q: "Does it replace my SSH server?",
    a: "No, it uses it. Paperboat carries the connection to the machine's own sshd, which never needs to listen on a public address.",
  },
  {
    q: "What do I see when something is wrong?",
    a: "The reason in plain words: no access, machine offline, SSH not set up, or sshd refusing. <code>pb ssh doctor studio</code> checks each step for you.",
  },
  {
    q: "How fast does it connect?",
    a: "Between two machines that have talked before, a shell is ready in under a second.",
  },
]
---

<Feature
  slug="ssh"
  title="SSH without keys or open ports | Paperboat"
  description="ssh, scp, sftp and rsync to every machine, with the keys handled for you and no port open on the internet."
  headline="SSH without the keys"
  faq={faq}
  related={["terminal", "files", "teams"]}
  compare={["ssh-bastion", "teleport", "tailscale"]}
>
  <p slot="lede">ssh, scp, sftp and rsync to every machine you own. Paperboat handles the keys, and no port is open to the internet.</p>
  <Term slot="aside" lines={["$ pb ssh studio", "ana@studio:~$", "", "$ pb rsync -a ./site/ studio:/srv/site/", "$ pb scp studio:app.log ."]} />

  <Beat id="tools-title" title="Your tools just work">
    <p>Every machine gets an SSH host name. VS Code, Cursor, Git and plain rsync use it like any other server.</p>
    <Term slot="visual" lines={[`$ ssh studio.${localDomain}`, `$ git clone studio.${localDomain}:app.git`, "# VS Code: Remote-SSH, then studio"]} />
  </Beat>

  <Beat id="access-title" title="Access you can take back" flip>
    <p>Give a teammate SSH to one machine. Take it away, and their open sessions end within seconds.</p>
    <Term slot="visual" lines={["$ pb ssh maya@staging", "Connected to staging", "# later: access removed", "Connection closed: access revoked"]} />
  </Beat>

  <section class="section section-rule" aria-labelledby="details-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="visually-hidden" id="details-title">Details</h2>
      <div class="points points-3">
        <div>
          <h3 class="h3">No open ports</h3>
          <p>sshd stays off the internet. The machine needs no public address.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="h3">Host keys checked</h3>
          <p>If a machine's key changes, pb stops and tells you before anything is sent.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="h3">In the audit log</h3>
          <p>Every session's start and end, with who and which machine.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Feature>
